---
import ComponentDoc from '../../layouts/ComponentDoc.astro';
import Section from '@esa/docs/Section.astro';
import Preview from '@esa/docs/Preview.astro';
import ApiTable from '../../components/ApiTable.astro';
import PropsTable from '@esa/docs/PropsTable.astro';
import Pill from '@esa/ecology/esa-pill.astro';

// Prose only — names, types and defaults are generated from the component
// source by src/data/component-api.ts, so this table cannot drift.
const describe = {
  label: "Required. Text shown inside the pill.",
  variant: "Color intent — drives background, text, and border.",
  size: "Pill height and text size.",
  removable: "Shows a remove (×) button.",
  category: "Project vocabulary this pill labels — emits data-category for a spoke-defined color ramp. See Custom colors.",
};

const slots = [
  { name: 'icon', type: 'slot', description: 'Leading inline SVG, rendered left of the label.' },
];

const events = [
  { name: 'removed', type: 'CustomEvent', description: 'Bubbles when the remove button is clicked; the pill then removes itself from the DOM.' },
];
---
<ComponentDoc name="Pill" category="Display" slug="esa-pill" type=".astro" status="stable"
  summary="Compact, rounded tag with color variants, sizes, an optional leading icon, and an optional remove control.">

  <Section id="preview" title="Preview">
    <Preview code={`<Pill label="Wetlands" variant="success" removable={false} />`}>
      <Pill label="Wetlands" variant="success" removable={false} />
    </Preview>
  </Section>

  <Section id="variants" title="Variants">
    <Preview code={`<Pill label="Default" variant="default" removable={false} />
<Pill label="Primary" variant="primary" removable={false} />
<Pill label="Success" variant="success" removable={false} />
<Pill label="Warning" variant="warning" removable={false} />
<Pill label="Danger" variant="danger" removable={false} />
<Pill label="Info" variant="info" removable={false} />`}>
      <Pill label="Default" variant="default" removable={false} />
      <Pill label="Primary" variant="primary" removable={false} />
      <Pill label="Success" variant="success" removable={false} />
      <Pill label="Warning" variant="warning" removable={false} />
      <Pill label="Danger" variant="danger" removable={false} />
      <Pill label="Info" variant="info" removable={false} />
    </Preview>
  </Section>

  <Section id="sizes" title="Sizes">
    <Preview code={`<Pill label="Extra small" size="xs" removable={false} />
<Pill label="Small" size="sm" removable={false} />
<Pill label="Medium" size="md" removable={false} />
<Pill label="Large" size="lg" removable={false} />`}>
      <Pill label="Extra small" size="xs" removable={false} />
      <Pill label="Small" size="sm" removable={false} />
      <Pill label="Medium" size="md" removable={false} />
      <Pill label="Large" size="lg" removable={false} />
    </Preview>
  </Section>

  <Section id="states" title="Icon & removable">
    <p>Pass a leading icon via the <code>icon</code> slot. With <code>removable</code> (the default), a × button emits a <code>removed</code> event and removes the pill from the DOM.</p>
    <Preview code={`<Pill label="Tagged" variant="primary" removable={false}>
  <svg slot="icon">…</svg>
</Pill>
<Pill label="Wetlands" variant="success" />
<Pill label="Overdue" variant="danger" />`}>
      <Pill label="Tagged" variant="primary" removable={false}>
        <svg slot="icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M12.586 2.586A2 2 0 0 0 11.172 2H4a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v7.172a2 2 0 0 0 .586 1.414l8.704 8.704a2.426 2.426 0 0 0 3.42 0l6.58-6.58a2.426 2.426 0 0 0 0-3.42z"></path>
          <circle cx="7.5" cy="7.5" r=".5" fill="currentColor"></circle>
        </svg>
      </Pill>
      <Pill label="Wetlands" variant="success" />
      <Pill label="Overdue" variant="danger" />
    </Preview>
  </Section>

  <Section id="custom-colors" title="Custom colors">
    <p>
      <code>variant</code> covers the six <strong>system intents</strong> and is deliberately closed —
      <code>success</code> means succeeded, not "green". A project's own vocabulary is an open set the
      hub can't enumerate: permit types, survey stages, species, funding sources. That's what
      <code>category</code> is for.
    </p>
    <p>
      Pass a category name and the pill emits <code>data-category</code>. Your theme scopes a
      three-step ramp to that name; the pill reads steps <strong>2 / 6 / 11</strong> for fill, border and
      text — the same triple every built-in variant uses, so your category renders as a native member
      of the set rather than a foreign object.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Pick a scale, don't pick colors.</strong> The hub already ships eleven full Radix scales
      as tier-1 primitives, twelve steps each. Point the three names at one of them and you're done —
      no hex anywhere:
    </p>
    <Preview code={`<Pill label="Permit expired" category="permit-expired" removable={false} />
<Pill label="Awaiting survey" category="awaiting-survey" removable={false} />

/* in your <project>-theme.css — one block per category */
[data-category="permit-expired"] {
  --category-2:  var(--color-teal-2);
  --category-6:  var(--color-teal-6);
  --category-11: var(--color-teal-11);
}`}>
      <Pill label="Permit expired" category="permit-expired" removable={false} />
      <Pill label="Awaiting survey" category="awaiting-survey" removable={false} />
      <Pill label="Prescribed burn" category="prescribed-burn" removable={false} />
    </Preview>
    <p>
      <strong>Start with <code>teal</code>, <code>gold</code> or <code>green</code>.</strong> Those three
      are the scales no semantic role has claimed, so they carry no borrowed meaning. The other eight —
      <code>grass</code>, <code>blue</code>, <code>lime</code>, <code>yellow</code>, <code>red</code>,
      <code>orange</code>, <code>copper</code>, <code>gray</code> — already back brand, info, success,
      warning and danger. Reusing one makes a category look like a status it isn't, which is worse than
      leaving it neutral.
    </p>
    <p>
      Two rungs down from there, in order. <strong>Need a hue we don't ship?</strong>
      <code>@radix-ui/colors</code> is already a dependency and carries all thirty scales —
      <code>@import '@radix-ui/colors/purple.css'</code> in your theme, then point at
      <code>--purple-2/6/11</code>. <strong>Need a brand color that isn't a Radix hue at all?</strong>
      Only then reach for
      <a href="https://www.radix-ui.com/colors/custom" rel="external">radix-ui.com/colors/custom</a>,
      which fits your color to a 12-step perceptual scale; copy steps 2, 6 and 11 and rename the
      <code>--accent-</code> prefix.
    </p>
    <p>
      All three rungs exist to avoid the same thing: a fill and a text color chosen independently. That
      is how dark purple ends up on near-black, and nothing in the build will tell you.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Know where the line is.</strong> Step 11 is tuned to APCA, not WCAG 2, so on step 2 it
      sits <em>at</em> the AA boundary rather than above it. Measured across all nine Radix scales the
      hub ships: <code>gold</code> 5.60, <code>red</code> 4.94, <code>grass</code> 4.82,
      <code>lime</code> 4.56, <code>blue</code> 4.53 — then <code>green</code> 4.49,
      <code>yellow</code> 4.42, <code>teal</code> 4.34 and <code>orange</code> 4.25, all under 4.5:1.
      Four of nine miss AA for normal text, and the rest pass by a hair.
    </p>
    <p>
      This is a property of the scale, not of this mechanism — the built-in <code>warning</code> variant
      measures 4.43 and always has. <strong>Step 12 clears AA on every scale at 10:1 or better</strong>,
      so a category carrying real weight should point <code>--category-11</code> at step 12 instead; the
      cost is a visibly darker label than the semantic pills beside it. Which step the system settles on
      is a question for the contrast pass, not one to answer per component.
    </p>
    <p>
      The three <code>--category-*</code> names are <strong>not hub tokens</strong> — your theme
      declares them, the component reads them, which is the inverse of every other token in the kit.
      That's deliberate: the mechanism is the hub's, the vocabulary is your project's. The
      <em>values</em> you point them at should still be hub tokens, which is the whole argument above.
      A category with no ramp defined, or a typo in the name, falls back to the default pill rather
      than losing the declaration; and because the ramp arrives as one block, fill and text can't be
      set independently.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="api" title="API">
    <ApiTable slug="esa-pill" describe={describe} />
    <h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">Slots</h3>
    <PropsTable rows={slots} />
    <h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">Events</h3>
    <PropsTable rows={events} />
  </Section>

  <Section id="accessibility" title="Accessibility">
    <ul class="a11y">
      <li>The remove button has <code>aria-label="Remove"</code>; the leading icon is <code>aria-hidden</code>.</li>
      <li>Remove click <code>stopPropagation()</code>s so it won't trigger a click on a surrounding interactive container.</li>
      <li>Color intent is reinforced by the label text — color is never the only signal.</li>
    </ul>
  </Section>

</ComponentDoc>

<!-- The three demo ramps for the Custom colors section. This stands in for a
     spoke's <project>-theme.css, which is where these belong in real use — the hub
     ships no --category-* token and this page is the one place in the repo that
     declares any.

     THE THREE UNCLAIMED SCALES, on purpose: teal, gold and green are the ones no
     semantic role references, so the demo is also the recommendation. These were
     pasted Radix hexes until the section was rewritten to lead with the shipped
     scales — a docs page arguing "point at a hub token, never a hex" while itself
     holding nine hexes teaches the hexes. `is:global` because Astro would
     otherwise scope these to this page's own elements and they would never reach
     the pill's [data-category] rule. -->
<style is:global>
  [data-category="permit-expired"]  { --category-2: var(--color-teal-2);  --category-6: var(--color-teal-6);  --category-11: var(--color-teal-11); }
  [data-category="awaiting-survey"] { --category-2: var(--color-gold-2);  --category-6: var(--color-gold-6);  --category-11: var(--color-gold-11); }
  [data-category="prescribed-burn"] { --category-2: var(--color-green-2); --category-6: var(--color-green-6); --category-11: var(--color-green-11); }
</style>
